    - analysis_quality  # ede7
    isbefore: []  # ede7
    duplicate_of: []  # ede7
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ede7
    pr_ref:  # ede7
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 while fixing WI-bivin-ronup-kuzam-giliz-sinoz-gihug-tigas-rovom.\n\nAn explicit generic instantiation call emits no calls edge at all. In go.py's call arm, callee_name is set only when the call_expression's function node is an identifier or a selector_expression; Map[int](1) and pkg.Map[int](1) have an index/generic-instantiation node there, so the call site vanishes from the graph (no bound edge, no unresolved placeholder). Live repro (analyze_go, dev 7a645c6c76 + bivin branch; package a with func Map[T any](x T) T, Use() { Map[int](1) }, Use2() { Map(2) }): Use2 -> a.go Map (ast_call); Use emits no calls edge.\n\nThis is the INV-guzuj / INV-foluz shape (a parsed call site that emits nothing) for a construct those fixes did not reach.\n\nNOT MEASURED: corpus frequency (explicit instantiation is uncommon next to inferred type arguments; count it before sizing). NOT CHECKED: the tree-sitter-go node type for each spelling (index_expression vs generic_type), and the same gap in the function-reference and struct-field-reference arms.\n\nACCEPTANCE: Map[int](x) and pkg.Map[int](x) emit the same calls edge as Map(x) / pkg.Map(x), resolved by the same rules (bare: caller's own package; qualified: the imported package)."  # ede7
    fields: {}  # ede7
- op: discuss  # 0d24
  at: '2026-10-04T01:40:03Z'  # 0d24
  by: agent  # 0d24
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0d24
  clock: 2  # 0d24
  nonce: 0d24  # 0d24
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (decontend stage 7), branch jgstern-agent/fix/vinuh, commit 8da3b291eb (local, not pushed; shared with WI-vinuh-tizad-lovum-bikir-fuzid-lovun-januz-nupig). Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/vinuh.md.\n\nPREMISE CORRECTION: tree-sitter-go spells an explicit instantiation two ways. ONE argument parses as a type_conversion_expression over a generic_type (Map[int](x), pkg.Map[int](x)) -- not a call_expression at all, because T[int](x) is also a generic TYPE conversion. Zero or several arguments parse as call_expression(function=index_expression) (Zero[int](), pkg.Zero[int]()). A type argument that can only be a type (F[[]int](a, b)) or several type args with several args parse as a plain call with type_arguments and always worked.\n\nFix: _go_instantiated_callee reads both shapes as the plain spelling; the call arm keys on callee_shape (identifier / selector) instead of the node type. Both shapes also spell a collection-element call (handlers[k](x)): silent as before -- a local by the bound-names rule, a selector on a value refused, a package variable by a kind check after resolution (only function/struct/interface/type instantiate). An unknown bare instantiation gets INV-guzuj's placeholder. Corpus: 94 new instantiation call sites (prometheus 10, otel-collector 84, alertmanager 0), read samples (sortFactoriesByType[exporter.Factory], newMemoryQueue[...], reflect.TypeFor[...], cache.AsLRU[...]) all correct. Residuals filed separately (generic function VALUES in the reference arms; a chain on a conversion-spelled instantiation)."  # 0d24
